Project stack:
- HTML
- CSS
- Vanilla JavaScript
- No frameworks or external libraries unless explicitly requested.

Project conventions:
- Keep the code simple and beginner-friendly.
- Use clear and descriptive variable and function names.
- Keep JavaScript in script.js and CSS in style.css.
- Use camelCase for JavaScript variable and function names.
- Reuse existing styles when possible instead of creating duplicate CSS rules.
- Keep the current visual style consistent when adding new features.
- Make only the changes required for the requested feature.

Safety:
- Never hardcode passwords, API keys, tokens, or credentials.
- Use textContent for user-provided text instead of innerHTML.
- Do not inject user input directly into HTML, URLs, or queries.

Things to avoid:
- Do not add unnecessary libraries, frameworks, or files.
- Do not rewrite working code unless it is necessary.
- Do not change existing functionality unless explicitly requested.
- Do not overcomplicate simple features.

Feature Sprint lesson:
- When adding a new feature, preserve all existing features and verify that they still work.